---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How Runtime Signals reviews and approves content before it publishes."
  canonicalPath="/editorial-policy"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Editorial policy</p>
    <h1>Review and approval</h1>
    <p>
      A piece moves through research and review — idea, researching, source-verified, outlined,
      drafting, technical review, editorial review — before it is ever eligible to publish. That
      workflow tracks readiness; it does not grant permission to publish.
    </p>
    <p>
      Publication authorization is separate and never comes from the content itself. It requires a
      merged, reviewed pull request whose required checks pass, whose CODEOWNERS approval is
      recorded, and whose deployment environment is authorized — captured for the exact commit being
      built. Nothing an author writes in a draft, including a status field, can grant that
      authorization.
    </p>
    <h2>AI assistance</h2>
    <p>
      LLMs may assist with source triage, metadata extraction, outline suggestions, citation-gap
      detection, and draft critique. No unreviewed AI-generated article is ever published; every
      AI-assisted step is recorded — model, prompt version, inputs, outputs, and the human
      reviewer's decision — and hidden reasoning is never stored.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      A correction does not erase history. It creates a visible revision note, keeps the article's
      stable URL, and states what changed and why. See <a href="/corrections">corrections</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-5) var(--space-9);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
  .prose h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-5);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }
</style>
